<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Sprint 28d Stage 9a (S9a.1) — the fixture that PREDICTS what the D3-direction
  round trip will do to a human's factory, before the Lombok-bearing slice of the
  fork is vendored to run it for real.

  It is shaped ON `com.iluwatar.saga.orchestration.ChapterResult`, which the
  survey names as the ONLY human-written self-returning factory in the fork whose
  constructor the AWAY leg can reach (package-private, and all twelve callers sit
  in that same package). Faithfully: a generic type, a two-argument constructor,
  and TWO factories that each fix one of those arguments to a different constant.

  WHAT THIS FIXTURE IS FOR, and its limit stated up front: it is a MECHANISM
  probe, not the D3 case. D3 asks for code we did not author, and this is
  authored — the same limit factory-target declares. Its job is to answer one
  question cheaply, on a shape we control: can the round trip close at all when
  the human's factory is a PARTIAL APPLICATION rather than a forwarder? If it
  cannot, that answer does not depend on the corpus and vendoring Lombok would
  not change it.

  No dependencies, so nothing here can fail to resolve and be read as a
  refactoring defect.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>org.jawata.fixtures</groupId>
    <artifactId>partial-factory</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>

    <properties>
        <maven.compiler.release>21</maven.compiler.release>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
    </properties>
</project>
